// read.mino.mobi — the deep-reading wing. Worker name `read`; the custom domain
// was attached in the dashboard rather than declared here, which meant a green
// `wrangler deploy` printed only
//
//     Deployed read triggers
//       https://read.majormobius.workers.dev
//
// with no mention of read.mino.mobi — so the run could not satisfy the golden
// rule (docs/DEPLOYS.md §4: verify the log binds `<domain> (custom domain)`).
// The deploy was in fact reaching production the whole time — verified by
// fetching the live assets and finding them byte-identical to HEAD — but a
// check that cannot distinguish a real deploy from a stray workers.dev deploy
// is not a check. Declaring the route here makes every future run
// self-verifying, and matches the other 50 of 60 wrangler configs in this repo.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "read",
  "main": "worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-03-14",
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "read.mino.mobi", "custom_domain": true }
  ],
  "assets": {
    "directory": ".",
    "binding": "ASSETS"
  }
}
